# Client-side env vars only. Both are safe to expose (VITE_ bundles them into shipped JS) —
# the anon key is meaningless without RLS, and RLS is enforced on every table (see
# supabase/migrations/20260817120000_enable_rls_core_tables.sql).
#
# DO NOT add another VITE_-prefixed secret to this file or to .env. Server-side secrets
# (GROQ_API_KEY, and anything else an Edge Function needs) belong in Supabase Edge Function
# secrets — `supabase secrets set NAME=value` — never in a client-bundled env var. This was the
# exact mistake that exposed the Groq key before this file existed; don't repeat it.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
